1.------REACT------
Keyword: Component-Based UI

React is a JavaScript library used to make interactive user interfaces for web applications.
It helps us build reusable components and update the webpage without reloading the whole page.
This is called a single page application, where users can move between different pages easily.


2.------JAVASCRIPT------
Keyword: Logic Building

JavaScript is a programming language used to add logic to websites.
It helps us perform calculations, make decisions, handle events and control how a website works.


3.------UI------
Keyword: Visual Interaction Layer

UI (User Interface) is the visual part of a website that users interact with.
It includes buttons, images, text and forms, making it easier for users to use the application.


4.------COMPONENTS-------
Keyword: Reusable UI Blocks

React App is a collection of components.
Each component handles a particular part of the webpage, like a navbar, button or login form. 
We can reuse the same component wherever needed.


5.------PROPS------
Keyword: Data Passing

Props are used to pass data from one component to another. 
Props act like function parameters. 
Pass data as key-value pairs when calling a component.
They help us share information, like names, images or other details, between components. 


6.------STATE------
Keyword: Changing Data

State is used to store information in a component. 
When the state changes, React updates the webpage automatically. 
For example, changing a counter value or showing and hiding a form.




